    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Dashboard 01 - Intro'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='800' maxwidth='1000' minheight='800' minwidth='1000' />
      <zones>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='10250' id='3' type-v2='text' w='69900' x='1200' y='1875'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='24'>   UK Online Retail II: A Forensics Project</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>─</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>────</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>───</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='14500' id='4' type-v2='text' w='97000' x='1400' y='11250'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18' italic='true'>Does a rotatable, interactive 3D drill-down actually help an analyst investigate data — or is it just a novelty?</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='27250' id='5' type-v2='text' w='60700' x='2300' y='27500'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>That question came before this dataset did. Before any RFM model, before any inventory sprint, before a single query was written — the only thing on the table was whether giving a stakeholder a chart they could rotate, zoom into, filter, and pull apart would let them find something a flat bar or a 2D scatter couldn&apos;t show them at all....</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='27000' id='6' type-v2='text' w='60200' x='28200' y='55875'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>...This project is the answer, built and tested end to end: forensic cleaning, six behavioral fields, a working Tableau dashboard, and 31 rotatable 3D exhibits — proving the method on a well-known, thoroughly-picked-over dataset on purpose, so nothing about the result could be credited to novel data.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='5875' id='7' type-v2='text' w='51100' x='46900' y='87250'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>It&apos;s built to reward scrutiny, not skimming. →</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
