    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Dashboard 04 - Cleaning Pass'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='800' maxwidth='1000' minheight='800' minwidth='1000' />
      <zones>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='7250' id='3' type-v2='text' w='49500' x='24500' y='2125'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='24'>The Cleaning Pass</run>
            <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>────</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>────────────</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>───────────</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>────────────</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>───────</run>
            <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='21000' id='4' type-v2='text' w='90400' x='4500' y='10625'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>Nothing in this project gets trusted until the foundation under it is forensically clean. That&apos;s not a style preference — it&apos;s the rule the rest of the project stands on. A finding built on a dirty table isn&apos;t a finding, no matter how good the chart looks.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='42000' id='5' type-v2='text' w='86800' x='5200' y='30500'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>The discipline is paralegal-grade, not just careful: nothing gets deleted, only segregated. Every revision is append-only, citing the specific query and title it corrects, with the original figure preserved right alongside the correction — never silently overwritten. Both sides of every real methodological fork get built and compared, not just the one that felt right. No finding ships on visual evidence alone; the chart can flag something worth investigating, but only SQL confirms it&apos;s real.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='26750' id='6' type-v2='text' w='87900' x='5200' y='68875'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>That standard gets applied to every one of 184 queries across this project</run>
            <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>— not just the ones that produced a headline number.</run>
            <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18'>What that discipline catches, in practice, shows up throughout the pages that follow.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
