    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Dashboard 05 - Ops IT Findings'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='800' maxwidth='1000' minheight='800' minwidth='1000' />
      <zones>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='9750' id='3' type-v2='text' w='54600' x='22300' y='1625'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='24'> Operations &amp; Data Collection</run>
            <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>────</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>────────────</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>────</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>────</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>───────────</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>────────────</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>───</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='90375' id='4' type-v2='text' w='97500' x='1000' y='8500'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='17'>Not every finding in this project came from what&apos;s </run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='17' italic='true'>in</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='17'> the data. Some came from what the data collection process itself was doing wrong — and those findings aren&apos;t for marketing or warehousing. They&apos;re for whoever owns the pipeline.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='17'>Data entry wasn&apos;t consistent.</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='17'> The same kind of value showed up formatted different ways depending on when or how it was entered — the kind of inconsistency that a cleaning pass has to catch by hand, every time, because there&apos;s nothing upstream enforcing a single format. Worth a hard look at whatever system or program is currently handling entry, and whether something with better built-in validation exists.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='17'>Cancellations and administrative codes weren&apos;t isolated.</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='17'> These weren&apos;t broken out into their own field — in some cases, there wasn&apos;t a dedicated field for them at all. They were buried inside data meant to represent standard transactions, which means every downstream query has to know to go looking for them instead of being able to filter cleanly.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='17'>Dates, and the data&apos;s structure generally, need rules.</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='17'> Formatting wasn&apos;t standardized, so parsing and validating dates became its own recurring task rather than a one-time setup. The same applies more broadly: the fields themselves need defined rules, not just whatever happened to get typed in.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='17'>None of this surfaced on the first pass. Each issue took its own round of investigative querying — sometimes two or three separate queries just to pin down what it actually was and what its parameters were, before it could be excluded or fixed. Three days went into that alone. A small set of upstream rules would give that time back to the next analyst before they ever open the file.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout auto-generated='true' name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
            <zone h='100000' id='26' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
