                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='17'>Not every finding in this project came from what&apos;s </run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='17' italic='true'>in</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='17'> the data. Some came from what the data collection process itself was doing wrong — and those findings aren&apos;t for marketing or warehousing. They&apos;re for whoever owns the pipeline.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='17'>Data entry wasn&apos;t consistent.</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='17'> The same kind of value showed up formatted different ways depending on when or how it was entered — the kind of inconsistency that a cleaning pass has to catch by hand, every time, because there&apos;s nothing upstream enforcing a single format. Worth a hard look at whatever system or program is currently handling entry, and whether something with better built-in validation exists.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
