    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Dashboard 06 - Customer RFM in 3D'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='800' maxwidth='1000' minheight='800' minwidth='1000' />
      <zones>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='94625' id='3' type-v2='text' w='95900' x='2500' y='2125'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='24'>Chapter Three: Customer RFM in 3D</run>
            <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──────────</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──────</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──────────</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──────</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──────────</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──────</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──────────</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──────</run>
            <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>Standard RFM</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'> — recency, frequency, monetary — is one of the most familiar models in retail analytics. Nothing new there. What&apos;s being tested is whether rotating it in 3D surfaces something a flat version wouldn&apos;t.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>It did, three times.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>The funnel holds — with a real exception.</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'> Average spend declines as recency increases, the pattern everyone expects. But rotating the cube surfaced a population that doesn&apos;t decay with it: 58 customers, each over 377 days since their last order, each still carrying at least £2,180.28 in net spend. Not noise, not missing data — a real, dormant, high-value population sitting outside the funnel&apos;s own logic. Lapsed, but never small — which is why the dashboard on the next page labels this tier </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>Lapsed Whale</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>The frequency spike is sharper than expected.</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'> Order frequency climbs with spend, as predicted — but not gradually across the top 15-20% of customers the way an initial read of the chart suggested. It spikes hard at the 90th percentile and above. The lockstep is real; it&apos;s just a smaller, steeper population than the first pass assumed.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>One point kept breaking the pattern — on purpose.</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'> A single customer sat visibly apart from the rest of the high-spend cluster while rotating the chart: 325 days of recency where every comparable customer sat at 0-38. Chasing it down uncovered a 74,215-unit order, cancelled 16 minutes after it was placed — a data artifact inflating that customer&apos;s gross spend to over £77,000 when real net spend was closer to £169. That&apos;s why every spend figure in this project, from here forward, uses </run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>net spend after cancellations</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'> — not the raw gross total, which this one customer alone proved could be wildly misleading. The chart didn&apos;t just show a number that looked wrong. Rotating it is what made the outlier visible in the first place.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout auto-generated='true' name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
            <zone h='100000' id='21' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
              <zone h='98000' id='20' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98400' x='800' y='1000'>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='94625' id='3' type-v2='text' w='95900' x='2500' y='2125'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='24'>Chapter Three: Customer RFM in 3D</run>
                    <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──────────</run>
                    <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──────</run>
                    <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──────────</run>
                    <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──────</run>
                    <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──────────</run>
                    <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──────</run>
                    <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──────────</run>
                    <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──────</run>
                    <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>Standard RFM</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'> — recency, frequency, monetary — is one of the most familiar models in retail analytics. Nothing new there. What&apos;s being tested is whether rotating it in 3D surfaces something a flat version wouldn&apos;t.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>It did, three times.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>The funnel holds — with a real exception.</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'> Average spend declines as recency increases, the pattern everyone expects. But rotating the cube surfaced a population that doesn&apos;t decay with it: 58 customers, each over 377 days since their last order, each still carrying at least £2,180.28 in net spend. Not noise, not missing data — a real, dormant, high-value population sitting outside the funnel&apos;s own logic. Lapsed, but never small — which is why the dashboard on the next page labels this tier </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>Lapsed Whale</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>The frequency spike is sharper than expected.</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'> Order frequency climbs with spend, as predicted — but not gradually across the top 15-20% of customers the way an initial read of the chart suggested. It spikes hard at the 90th percentile and above. The lockstep is real; it&apos;s just a smaller, steeper population than the first pass assumed.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>One point kept breaking the pattern — on purpose.</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'> A single customer sat visibly apart from the rest of the high-spend cluster while rotating the chart: 325 days of recency where every comparable customer sat at 0-38. Chasing it down uncovered a 74,215-unit order, cancelled 16 minutes after it was placed — a data artifact inflating that customer&apos;s gross spend to over £77,000 when real net spend was closer to £169. That&apos;s why every spend figure in this project, from here forward, uses </run>
                    <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>net spend after cancellations</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'> — not the raw gross total, which this one customer alone proved could be wildly misleading. The chart didn&apos;t just show a number that looked wrong. Rotating it is what made the outlier visible in the first place.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='8' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
          </zones>
        </devicelayout>
      </devicelayouts>
      <simple-id uuid='{56F2E50F-71A2-4606-BFAE-37BA95991032}' />
    </dashboard>
    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Dashboard Chapter Five: Same Discipline, Different Domain'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='800' maxwidth='1000' minheight='800' minwidth='1000' />
      <zones>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='81125' id='3' type-v2='text' w='92800' x='2300' y='15000'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='16'>The full inventory, laid out.</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='16'>Æ </run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='16' italic='true'>(inventory_signal_3d.html)</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='16'> Every SKU, plotted by recency and monetary value the same way customers were — the same shape of question, asked of stock instead of people.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='16'>572 SKUs are overdue for restock.</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='16'>Æ </run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='16' italic='true'>(overdue_restock_standalone_3d.html)</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='16'> Items still selling, still moving, sitting below the threshold that should have triggered a reorder already.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='16'>201 SKUs looked like dead stock — until the season was checked.</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='16'>Æ </run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='16' italic='true'>(dead_stock_seasonal_deepdive_3d.html)</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='16'> A straightforward dormancy read would have written off all 201 as dead inventory. Checking each one against its own seasonal pattern first found that 93 of them aren&apos;t dead at all — they&apos;re seasonal, dormant right now because it isn&apos;t their season yet, not because nobody wants them. Writing those off would have meant re-purchasing inventory the warehouse already had sitting on a shelf.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='8500' id='4' type-v2='text' w='83500' x='9100' y='1000'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='24'>Chapter Five: Same Discipline, Different Domain</run>
            <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>────</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────</run>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>──</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='14500' id='5' type-v2='text' w='95000' x='2400' y='11250'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='16'>Everything up to this point has been about customers. The same forensic discipline, pointed at stock instead, turned out to hold just as much value — nobody set out looking for it in advance; it surfaced once the method was already proven and the same table got looked at from a different angle.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone h='5500' id='6' name='Link - Inventory Signal' show-title='false' w='19500' x='20200' y='38625' />
        <zone h='2875' id='7' name='Link - Overdue Restock' show-title='false' w='16000' x='83800' y='53750' />
        <zone h='3625' id='8' name='Link - Dead Stock' show-title='false' w='13300' x='55500' y='81375' />
