    <dashboard enable-sort-zone-taborder='true' name='Dashboard Confirmed From Two Directions'>
      <style />
      <size maxheight='800' maxwidth='1000' minheight='800' minwidth='1000' />
      <zones>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='95875' id='3' type-v2='text' w='90300' x='2700' y='2000'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>Chapter Three found a seasonal cohort by studying customers — 618 people who all first purchased in the same three-month window, October through December 2010, in numbers too small and too tightly clustered to be random.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>Chapter Five found the same signal by studying stock — 93 SKUs that looked like dead inventory until their sales pattern was checked against the calendar, and turned out to be seasonal, not dormant.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>Two completely different questions, asked with two different methods, pointed at two different slices of the same table — and they landed on the same real pattern from opposite directions. Neither one set out to confirm the other. That&apos;s what makes it hold up: a coincidence explains one seasonal finding. It doesn&apos;t explain two, found independently, agreeing with each other.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>It traces back to a decision made in Chapter One, before either finding existed: 228,297 rows with no customer ID attached — not errors, just legitimate transactions missing an identifier — got cleaned and preserved instead of deleted. Nothing about that decision looked like it would matter later. It sat there, untouched, for chapters. And it&apos;s part of why the foundation under both findings held up when it mattered.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>This is what the whole project was actually testing, going all the way back to the question on page one: not whether 3D looks impressive, but whether the discipline underneath it — clean once, verify twice, never delete — actually pays for itself. It did. Twice, independently, without being asked to.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone forceUpdate='true' h='6875' id='4' type-v2='text' w='92900' x='1500' y='4750'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='24'>Confirmed From Two Directions</run>
            <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <devicelayouts>
        <devicelayout auto-generated='true' name='Phone'>
          <size maxheight='700' minheight='700' sizing-mode='vscroll' />
          <zones>
            <zone h='100000' id='12' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
              <zone h='98000' id='11' param='vert' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98400' x='800' y='1000'>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='95875' id='3' type-v2='text' w='90300' x='2700' y='2000'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>Chapter Three found a seasonal cohort by studying customers — 618 people who all first purchased in the same three-month window, October through December 2010, in numbers too small and too tightly clustered to be random.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>Chapter Five found the same signal by studying stock — 93 SKUs that looked like dead inventory until their sales pattern was checked against the calendar, and turned out to be seasonal, not dormant.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>Two completely different questions, asked with two different methods, pointed at two different slices of the same table — and they landed on the same real pattern from opposite directions. Neither one set out to confirm the other. That&apos;s what makes it hold up: a coincidence explains one seasonal finding. It doesn&apos;t explain two, found independently, agreeing with each other.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>It traces back to a decision made in Chapter One, before either finding existed: 228,297 rows with no customer ID attached — not errors, just legitimate transactions missing an identifier — got cleaned and preserved instead of deleted. Nothing about that decision looked like it would matter later. It sat there, untouched, for chapters. And it&apos;s part of why the foundation under both findings held up when it mattered.</run>
                    <run>Æ&#10;&#10;&#10;</run>
                    <run fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='14'>This is what the whole project was actually testing, going all the way back to the question on page one: not whether 3D looks impressive, but whether the discipline underneath it — clean once, verify twice, never delete — actually pays for itself. It did. Twice, independently, without being asked to.</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
                <zone forceUpdate='true' h='6875' id='4' type-v2='text' w='92900' x='1500' y='4750'>
                  <formatted-text>
                    <run fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='24'>Confirmed From Two Directions</run>
                    <run fontalignment='1'>Æ&#10;</run>
                    <run bold='true' fontalignment='1' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────</run>
                  </formatted-text>
                  <zone-style>
                    <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                    <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                    <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                    <format attr='margin' value='4' />
                    <format attr='padding' value='0' />
                  </zone-style>
                </zone>
              </zone>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='8' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
          </zones>
        </devicelayout>
      </devicelayouts>
      <simple-id uuid='{D87FC4DC-A887-4526-9A28-25F78A59007B}' />
